Takeaways:
- Again my stones formed a long center wall (D4-J4, D5-E5, C6-D7) that scored very little.
  Black just took two opposite corners (G7 then C4) and lived easily on both.
- After W E5 / B F5 attach, my F4/G4/E4 shape was slow; Black kept sente and invaded C4.
  Better as White vs a 3-3-ish G7: take a corner myself (C3 or C4/D3) instead of tengen,
  or after F5 attach play solidly but then grab the open lower-left corner (C3/C4) FIRST.
- J6 blunder: I extended a stone into a spot where the 2-stone group had a single liberty.
  Before each move, count the liberties of the stone I'm placing AND its group after placement.
- H7 cut was over-ambitious (2 libs vs their many); read races before cutting.

